# Naming: Job, Handler, View

| Layer | Names | Belongs in |
|-------|--------|------------|
| **Job** | Business case (may include vendor/product) | Config `name`, matching rules |
| **Handler** | Execution strategy only | `*Handler` class + `handlerType` |
| **View** | Result presentation contract | `*View` + `viewType` |

## Rules

- Do **not** put company/vendor names in handler or view type names.
- Prefer a new **job config** entry when an existing handler + view already fit.
- Add a new **`IJobHandler`** only when the execution path or result contract cannot be expressed by config.
- Add a new **view** when the UI for `JobResult` differs.
- Prefer job config for result title/type metadata; avoid hard-coding vendor strings in generic handlers.

## Examples

- Good handler: `PythonScriptHandler`
- Avoid: `AteaInvoiceHandler` (legacy name; rename when touching that area)
- Good job name: `"Atea Invoice License"`
- Good view: `GridAndCommentView`

Details and checklists: `DEVELOPMENT.md`.
